================================================================================
                                 PREAMBLE
================================================================================

The Cluaiz Source-Available License (CSL) is designed to cultivate a high-performance,
collaborative ecosystem. By making our source code visible and adaptable, we empower
individual developers, startups, researchers, and hobbyists to build freely. At the 
same time, this license requires fair commercial participation from large-scale 
enterprises and protects the platform from competing hosted clones.

This is a SOURCE-AVAILABLE license. It is NOT an OSI-approved Open Source license.
It offers a balanced "Open-Core" model: completely free for personal, educational, 
startup, and local self-hosted use, with commercial licensing required for large 
enterprises and managed service providers.

================================================================================
1. DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

"Licensed Software" means the source code, build scripts, configuration files, 
and documentation of the Cluaiz ecosystem made available under this License.

"Enterprise" means any corporate entity, business, or organization (including 
its parent company, subsidiaries, and controlled affiliates) whose annual gross 
revenue exceeded Ten Million USD ($10,000,000 USD) in its preceding fiscal year.

"Contributor" means any individual or corporate entity that has authored and 
successfully merged at least one non-trivial contribution (minimum of 50 lines of 
functional code, critical bug fixes, or equivalent extensive documentation) into 
the official upstream repository of the Licensed Software.

"Competing SaaS / Hosted Service" means any service that provides the core 
functional features of the Licensed Software as a hosted platform, managed API, 
managed container, or cloud offering in direct commercial competition with the 
official cloud services or commercial API endpoints hosted by Cluaiz.

================================================================================
2. LICENSE GRANTS
================================================================================

Subject to the terms and conditions of this License, Cluaiz Technologies hereby 
grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free, non-transferable license to 
view, modify, copy, and distribute the Licensed Software under the following tiers:

A. Developer & Startup Tier (Free Use)
--------------------------------------
You may use the Licensed Software for personal projects, academic research, 
education, local evaluation, and within business operations, provided that:
  (1) You are not an Enterprise (as defined in Section 1).
  (2) You do not operate a Competing SaaS / Hosted Service (as defined in Section 1).

B. Contributor Commercial Waiver
--------------------------------
In appreciation of community support, any verified Contributor is granted a perpetual, 
worldwide, royalty-free Commercial License to use, modify, and run the core Licensed 
Software for commercial operations, fully bypassing the Enterprise revenue threshold, 
provided that:
  (1) The Contributor remains in good standing within the community.
  (2) The Contributor's usage does not involve operating a Competing SaaS / Hosted Service.

================================================================================
3. ENTERPRISE COMMERCIAL MANDATE
================================================================================

If you are an Enterprise, you may evaluate the Licensed Software in a non-production 
environment for up to thirty (30) days. Continued or production use of the Licensed 
Software within an Enterprise requires a separate, written Enterprise Commercial Agreement 
or Strategic Partnership Agreement from Cluaiz Technologies.

================================================================================
4. PROTECTIVE COVENANTS & RESTRICTIONS
================================================================================

A. No Competing Managed Services
--------------------------------
You may not use, package, or distribute the Licensed Software to operate, host, 
or offer a Competing SaaS / Hosted Service or commercial API clone. Offering Cluaiz 
as a managed cloud utility requires a specific hosting provider agreement.

B. Proprietary Methodology Protection
-------------------------------------
The Licensed Software contains proprietary algorithms, state-probing methodologies, 
and mathematical frameworks (including but not limited to the AtmaSteer Protocol, 
Engine C logical interfaces, and Silicon Probing signatures). While the source code 
is public and licensed under these terms, these methodologies are protected by copyright, 
trademarks, and patents (where applicable). You may not extract or isolate these 
proprietary methodologies to construct a competing closed-source binary or platform.

C. Trademark Separation
-----------------------
This License does not grant any rights to use the trademarked names "Cluaiz", 
"Cluaiz-OS", "Archer", "Antigravity", or any associated official logos. Any 
redistribution, fork, or derivative work of the Licensed Software must be renamed 
to a distinct brand that does not imply affiliation with or endorsement by Cluaiz.

